<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GOLDFIELDS GHANA LIFTS YR INCOME.</title>
<headline>GOLDFIELDS GHANA LIFTS YR INCOME.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million US$ unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Costs applicable to sales  14.72	vs    12.73</p>
<p>    Net income			1.73	vs    0.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   2.48	vs    1.47</p>
<p>    Tax				 0.76	vs    0.52 </p>
<p>    Interest and other	    0.12	vs    0.12</p>
<p>    Capital expenditure	   0.75	vs    0.56</p>
<p>    Sales			    18.56	vs    15.29</p>
<p>Full name: Goldfields Ghana Ltd </p>
<p>    Tonnes milled		   287,370   vs    229,558</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said a feasibility study on the new</p>
<p>surface mine has confirmed the viability of the initial project</p>
<p>which would now proceed. The timing was subject to successful</p>
<p>conclusion of the agreements with the remaining property owners</p>
<p>in the mining area, and the normal government permits and mining</p>
<p>titles.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
